<title>UK: British Energy May sales up 7.6 pct.</title>
<headline>British Energy May sales up 7.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear electricity producer British Energy Plc said on Wednesday that total sales reached 6.51 Terawatt hours (TWh) in May from 6.05 a year ago.</p>
<p>A Terawatt hour is the largest unit of measurement for electricity sales, representing one billion kilowatt hours.</p>
<p>The following table details sales from each power station in TWh:</p>
<p>					 1997		   1996</p>
<p>    Station		     MAY   YEAR	   MAY   YEAR</p>
<p>					   TO DATE		TO DATE</p>
<p>    Hinkley Point B	  0.89   1.71	  0.77   1.65</p>
<p>    Hunterston B	     0.72   1.55	  0.62   1.13</p>
<p>    Dungeness B		0.70   1.30	  0.59   1.16</p>
<p>    Heysham 1		  0.84   1.46	  0.68   1.14</p>
<p>    Hartlepool		 0.71   1.31	  0.75   1.54</p>
<p>    Torness		    0.92   1.58	  0.79   1.66</p>
<p>    Heysham 2		  0.85   1.64	  0.97   1.73</p>
<p>    Sizewell B		 0.88   1.75	  0.88   1.74</p>
<p>    Total			6.51  12.30	  6.05  11.76</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
